    "method": "All 185 concordia plates read on 47 sheets at 776 px (runs/qc/plate_sheets/concordia). No identifiable real face -- every human figure is a back, a silhouette or a distant figure. No legible glyph, no watermark, no wrong-country signage (the film IS set in Italy, so Italian architecture is correct here). Funnels checked at 1600 px on N183 and N147: plain white, NO company mark, so the yellow cast on some plates is sunset light and not a real operator's livery. CORRECTED 2026-08-26 from a first pass that rejected four plates as period drift: all four are ship's CLINOMETERS, which is the right instrument and the film's own motif -- a ship that lists. The fault is only the OPEN-FLAME OIL LANTERN the prompt put beside three of them. N116 has no lantern and is accepted."
